
"""
Pilot Qwen3-VL rupture-salience fine-tuning for PROTECT-AI.

What this script does
---------------------
1. Reads the merged 3RS segment-level coder CSV.
2. Aggregates double-rated labels by 1-minute segment:
      WD_P_mean = mean patient-withdrawal salience
      CF_P_mean = mean patient-confrontation salience
3. Builds a SMALL patient-level pilot split (train/val/test).
4. Resolves the corresponding full-session videos recursively under VIDEO_ROOT.
5. Uses the existing patient-side role cache when available.
6. Samples chronological frames from the labelled 1-minute interval.
7. Crops the patient using YuNet face detections + cached left/right side.
8. Loads Qwen/Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct in 4-bit.
9. Applies LoRA to the language-model attention projections.
10. Uses the multimodal backbone hidden state + a small regression head to predict:
       WD_P_mean, CF_P_mean
11. Optimizes Huber loss and evaluates MAE / Spearman / rupture-any metrics.

IMPORTANT PILOT DESIGN
----------------------
- Patient-only visual input -> predicts patient targets only (WD_P, CF_P).
- Labels are kept continuous (e.g. 3.5), not rounded.
- Split is by patient_id to avoid leakage.
- Default pilot uses 8 patients and <= 15 segments/patient (~120 segments max).
- Default visual input is 32 frames ACROSS the full 60-second labelled segment.
  This is intentionally smaller than the final 4 x 15s x 32-frame setup so that
  the first LoRA experiment is feasible on a 32 GB RTX 5090.
- Once the pipeline works, increase temporal capacity or move to 4-window MIL.

Expected environment
--------------------
Use the existing .venv_molmo2 environment with:
  transformers >= 4.57
  torch with CUDA 12.8 support
  peft >= 0.17
  bitsandbytes
  opencv-python
  pandas
  scipy
  scikit-learn
"""

